345 - Christ Is the World's True Light
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 345
Topic: Christian Church - 

Verse 1:
[C]Christ is the world’s true light,
[Dm]Its captain of salva [Em]tion,
[C]The daystar [F]clear and bright
[F#m]Of every man and na tion;
[G]New life, new hope [G7/F]awakes
[Em]Where’er men [G7/B]own His sway:
[C]Freedom her [G7]bondage breaks,
[C]And night is turned to day.

Verse 2:
[C]In Christ all races meet,
[Dm]Their ancient feuds forgeting,
[C]The whole round [F]world complete,
[F#m]From sunrise to its setting:
[G]When Christ is [G7/F]throned as Lord,
[Em]Men shall forsake [G7/B]their fear,
[C]To plowshare [G7]beat the sword,
[C]To pruning hook the spear.

Verse 3:
[C]One Lord, in one great name
[Dm]Unite us all who [Em]own Thee,
[C]Cast out our [F]pride and shame
[F#m]That hinder to enthrone Thee;
[G]The world has [G7/F]waited long,
[Em]Has travailed [G7/B]long in pain,
[C]To heal its [G7]ancient wrong,
[C]Come, Prince of Peace, and reign.
